#+TITLE: REM rejects real operands required by SCHMS arc geometry
#+STATUS: NEXT
#+PRIORITY: P2
#+TYPE: compatibility
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: -
#+DATE: 2026-10-29

* Minimal reproduction

Run the adjacent =rem-real-operands-repro.lsp= with:

#+begin_src sh
clautolisp --no-init --host cador --dialect bricscad-v26 \
  -l issues/open/rem-real-operands-repro.lsp
#+end_src

Observed with the locally installed SBCL binary 2.3.73:
=REM expects a 32-bit AutoLISP integer, got 12.0d0.=

The inspected master 38af2d74 (release source 2.3.76) still defines
=builtin-rem= in =clautolisp/autolisp-builtins-core/source/api.lisp=
with =require-int32= on both operands. This is a source inspection, not a
claim that a newly built 2.3.76 binary was tested.

* Native contract and affected code

Autodesk documents integer or real operands and a real return if any
operand is real. It also documents zero, one and multiple operands:
[[https://help.autodesk.com/cloudhelp/2026/ENU/AutoCAD-AutoLISP-Reference/files/GUID-4CC43BEB-3215-41AE-839B-2DCE6354241A.htm][rem (AutoLISP), Autodesk reference]].

Actual SCHMS source: =src-vlx/voies-chainage.lsp=, =schms_mod2pi=,
called by =schms_split_bulge=. Seven newly prepared mathematical regression
cases fail at REM (normalization, signed semicircles, asymmetric splits,
transformation and endpoints). The existing 242-test unit baseline remains
separate. No workaround to the valid product math or relaxed assertion is
introduced. The nine candidate geometry tests (two pass, seven error) are
kept explicitly pending in SCHMS =tests/warning-sites/pending/=.

* Acceptance criteria

Accept real and mixed integer/real operands, preserve numeric return types,
and verify negative dividends/divisors, exact multiples and zero divisors
against the native contract. Cover zero, one and multiple operands too;
the current two-argument function signature is another contract gap to
verify, not something exercised by this minimal reproducer. Add language
regressions for the supported dialects and run the SCHMS candidate geometry
suite after updating the installed runtime. No CAD automation is necessary
for the minimal failure.

* Fixed 2026-10-29 (core) -- clautolisp 2.3.77, branch fix-rem-real-operands

builtin-rem (api.lisp) was int-only (require-int32 on two operands); it now
takes integer OR real operands and is variadic, reduced left to right. The
result is real when any operand is real (CL REM's float contagion), integer
when all are integers; the remainder follows the dividend's sign (truncated
division: (rem -7 2) = -1, (rem 7 -2) = 1, as both products do). REM registers
via make-core-builtin-subr like / and gcd, so the &rest signature made it
variadic with no registration change. Division by zero still signals as before.

Language regressions added to builtin-basic-arithmetic (the minimal repro's
(rem 12.0 16) -> 12.0 REAL, plus mixed, negative, variadic (rem 42 12 3) -> 0,
one-operand, and type assertions); builtin-basic-arithmetic + the div-by-zero
test green (fiveam 57/57).

Remaining (kept open until done):
  - run the SCHMS candidate geometry suite against the rebuilt 2.3.77 runtime
    (external; needs the SCHMS checkout) and un-pend the seven cases;
  - verify on a live product the exact value for ZERO and ONE operand (SPEC-
    UNCERTAIN in the source) and REAL zero-divisor behaviour (the fix keeps the
    integer div-by-zero signal; a real 0.0 divisor is not yet pinned to vendor).
